{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgANfs6eh4x8R4b4xhDwx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed Hijack so it works after headers have been sent, as long as no body has been written yet. The changes are in the working tree and not committed.\n\n**The problem:** `Hijack()` refused whenever `Written()` was true, and that includes the case where only headers were sent (for example after `WriteHeaderNow()`). That broke WebSocket libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket`.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `response_writer.go`: `Hijack()` now refuses only when body bytes have been written (`size > 0`). It still works before anything is written or after headers only. I added a short comment explaining why. I also changed the error text from \"gin: response already written\" to \"gin: response body already written\", since writing headers alone no longer triggers it.\n- `response_writer_test.go`: added a test case where `WriteHeaderNow()` is called and then hijacking is expected to succeed.\n\n**Verified:**\n- The new test case failed before the fix, with the expected `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n- It passes after the fix.\n- With only `response_writer.go` reverted (stashed), the new test fails again.\n- `go vet` and `gofmt -l` report nothing, and `go test ./...` passes in all packages.\n\n**Public behaviour change:** calling `Hijack()` after `WriteHeaderNow()` used to return an error and now succeeds. The error message text also changed.\n\nShould I commit it as `fix(response): refine hijack behavior for response lifecycle`?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":329,"cache_read_input_tokens":40040,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":329,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":482,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c80f1a0-d572-4027-9af5-86354c447f95","uuid":"ef37a874-4f2a-40e7-8a04-e93c8321aa32","timestamp":"2026-10-18T20:59:30.330Z","request_id":"req_011CgANfrsknhfAfd5CvCRuw"}
{"duration_api_ms":29195,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0c80f1a0-d572-4027-9af5-86354c447f95","total_cost_usd":0.30468080000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40369,"cache_read_input_tokens":224399,"output_tokens":2895,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":980},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":40369},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":482,"cache_read_input_tokens":40040,"cache_creation_input_tokens":329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":329,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":2895,"cacheReadInputTokens":224399,"cacheCreationInputTokens":40369,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.30468080000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":980,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":9,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I fixed Hijack so it works after headers have been sent, as long as no body has been written yet. The changes are in the working tree and not committed.\n\n**The problem:** `Hijack()` refused whenever `Written()` was true, and that includes the case where only headers were sent (for example after `WriteHeaderNow()`). That broke WebSocket libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket`.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `response_writer.go`: `Hijack()` now refuses only when body bytes have been written (`size > 0`). It still works before anything is written or after headers only. I added a short comment explaining why. I also changed the error text from \"gin: response already written\" to \"gin: response body already written\", since writing headers alone no longer triggers it.\n- `response_writer_test.go`: added a test case where `WriteHeaderNow()` is called and then hijacking is expected to succeed.\n\n**Verified:**\n- The new test case failed before the fix, with the expected `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n- It passes after the fix.\n- With only `response_writer.go` reverted (stashed), the new test fails again.\n- `go vet` and `gofmt -l` report nothing, and `go test ./...` passes in all packages.\n\n**Public behaviour change:** calling `Hijack()` after `WriteHeaderNow()` used to return an error and now succeeds. The error message text also changed.\n\nShould I commit it as `fix(response): refine hijack behavior for response lifecycle`?","ttft_ms":5060,"type":"result","duration_ms":42163,"uuid":"4cb0d347-0d73-4965-99d3-37f1811d161d","ttft_stream_ms":938,"time_to_request_ms":235,"first_content_frame_ms":939,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
